            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Unfortunately, working with system register is indeed a bit messy. The reason (I think) is mostly because it is something shared by both instances and that Neovim has special treatment of system clipboard (see `:h clipboard`).\r\n\r\nHere is [one example of how I get over it](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/59ecf78491f29a9ec31f4124f3da77091f37e4d9/tests/test_extra.lua#L2841-L2851).\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\n> ```\r\n> ...\r\n> child.type_keys('<leader>cc') -- copy name 'SfProject' into \"*\" registration\r\n> ...\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThe answer would have been more helpful if you posted a fully reproducible (and small-ish) test case. For example, the following test case passes locally for me:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nT['tmp'] = function()\r\n  child.fn.setreg('*', 'Hello')\r\n  eq(child.fn.getreg('*'), 'Hello')\r\nend\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Unfortunately, working with system register is indeed a bit messy. The reason (I think) is mostly because it is something shared by both instances and that Neovim has special treatment of system clipboard (see <code class=\"notranslate\">:h clipboard</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/59ecf78491f29a9ec31f4124f3da77091f37e4d9/tests/test_extra.lua#L2841-L2851\">one example of how I get over it</a>.</p>\n<hr>\n<blockquote>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"...\nchild.type_keys('&lt;leader&gt;cc') -- copy name 'SfProject' into &quot;*&quot; registration\n...\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">...\nchild.type_keys('&lt;leader&gt;cc') -- copy name 'SfProject' into \"*\" registration\n...\n</code></pre></div>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The answer would have been more helpful if you posted a fully reproducible (and small-ish) test case. For example, the following test case passes locally for me:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"T['tmp'] = function()\n  child.fn.setreg('*', 'Hello')\n  eq(child.fn.getreg('*'), 'Hello')\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">T</span>[<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>tmp<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">child</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">setreg</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>*<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Hello<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">eq</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">child</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">getreg</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>*<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>), <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Hello<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "Unfortunately, working with system register is indeed a bit messy. The reason (I think) is mostly because it is something shared by both instances and that Neovim has special treatment of system clipboard (see :h clipboard).\nHere is one example of how I get over it.\n\n\n...\nchild.type_keys('<leader>cc') -- copy name 'SfProject' into \"*\" registration\n...\n\n\nThe answer would have been more helpful if you posted a fully reproducible (and small-ish) test case. For example, the following test case passes locally for me:\nT['tmp'] = function()\n  child.fn.setreg('*', 'Hello')\n  eq(child.fn.getreg('*'), 'Hello')\nend",
